From 92ba3307431a1756a3c8094787527a38ce19623d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Date: Wed, 4 Mar 2026 11:54:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] net: cadence: macb: enable EEE for Raspberry Pi RP1
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Set MACB_CAPS_EEE for the Raspberry Pi 5 RP1 southbridge
(Cadence GEM_GXL rev 0x00070109 paired with BCM54213PE PHY).

EEE has been verified on RP1 hardware: the LPI counter registers
at 0x270-0x27c return valid data, the TXLPIEN bit in NCR (bit 19)
controls LPI transmission correctly, and ethtool --show-eee reports
the negotiated state after link-up.

Other GEM variants that share the same LPI register layout (SAMA5D2,
SAME70, PIC32CZ) can be enabled by adding MACB_CAPS_EEE to their
respective config entries once tested.

Reviewed-by: Claudiu Beznea <claudiu.beznea@tuxon.dev>
Reviewed-by: Théo Lebrun <theo.lebrun@bootlin.com>
Signed-off-by: Nicolai Buchwitz <nb@tipi-net.de>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260304105432.631186-5-nb@tipi-net.de
Signed-off-by: Jakub Kicinski <kuba@kernel.org>
---
[ Talos backport note (not part of the upstream commit message):
  Cherry-picked from mainline commit 92ba3307431a ("net: cadence: macb:
  enable EEE for Raspberry Pi RP1"), merged in Linux 7.1, onto 6.18.41.

  One context conflict was resolved.  Upstream extends a .caps field
  ending in MACB_CAPS_GEM_HAS_PTP, but in this tree
  0001-net-macb-flush-PCIe-posted-write-after-TSTART-doorbe.patch has
  already appended MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES to
  raspberrypi_rp1_config.  MACB_CAPS_EEE is appended after it, so the
  combined result is:

      MACB_CAPS_GIGABIT_MODE_AVAILABLE | MACB_CAPS_CLK_HW_CHG |
      MACB_CAPS_JUMBO | MACB_CAPS_GEM_HAS_PTP |
      MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES | MACB_CAPS_EEE

  Note for reviewers: applied with GNU patch's default fuzz factor, the
  unmodified upstream hunk applies *successfully* to mpfs_config
  (Microchip PolarFire SoC) roughly 40 lines earlier, which shares the
  trailing "MACB_CAPS_GEM_HAS_PTP," context line.  That would enable EEE
  on the wrong SoC, leave RP1 untouched, and exit 0.  The rebased hunk
  in this patch has exact context and cannot fuzz-match elsewhere. ]

  drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c | 3 ++-
  1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
index 04791fd..bc14e16 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/cadence/macb_main.c
@@ -5728,7 +5728,8 @@ static const struct macb_config raspberrypi_rp1_config = {
 	.caps = MACB_CAPS_GIGABIT_MODE_AVAILABLE | MACB_CAPS_CLK_HW_CHG |
 		MACB_CAPS_JUMBO |
 		MACB_CAPS_GEM_HAS_PTP |
-		MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES,
+		MACB_CAPS_PCIE_POSTED_WRITES |
+		MACB_CAPS_EEE,
 	.dma_burst_length = 16,
 	.clk_init = macb_clk_init,
 	.init = macb_init,
